1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,040
If you have a kessia, wear it.

2
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:07,580
So I went to the mall yesterday and I live in a neighborhood that has a large Zionist community.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:13,440
And I wore mine proudly to the mall knowing somebody could sneer at me.

4
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:15,740
You know, somebody might say something off the side of their neck.

5
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:17,840
More bold, somebody might try to star something.

6
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,480
Mama say, mama say, mama say, mama go say.

7
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:20,440
So I was ready.

8
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:22,740
You know what I got instead?

9
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:24,880
I got love.

10
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:28,800
I had three different people stop me and say, thank you.

11
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,580
Thank you. Thank you for wearing your kessia.

12
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:33,420
It was a younger woman, a man.

13
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:34,660
He stopped and gave me a dap.

14
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:36,960
And an older woman gave me a thumbs up.

15
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,860
She said, I see this.

16
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:39,680
I see this.

17
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:40,960
Thank you. Thank you.

18
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:46,120
So we must always represent for the community that we support.

19
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:49,380
Even when we feel like we're the lone soldier in the situation.

20
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:54,940
And when we see somebody else representing, we must always acknowledge them.

21
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:57,660
So we can always know where we are and who we're with.

